.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-mcp-wait 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-mcp\-wait \- Poll one declared method until its declared reduction changes, or until an eviction limit less a buffer passes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten mcp wait\fR [\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-\-evict\-after\fR] [\fB\-\-buffer\fR] [\fB\-\-singleton\fR] [\fB\-\-each\-receipt\fR] [\fB\-\-arg\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIserver\fR> <\fImethod\fR> [\fIparams\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Poll one declared method until its declared reduction changes, or until an eviction limit less a buffer passes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<interval>\fR
Seconds between polls (default 30)
.TP
\fB\-\-evict\-after\fR \fI<evict\-after>\fR
The host\*(Aqs cache\-eviction limit in seconds; absent, the wait ends only on a change
.TP
\fB\-\-buffer\fR \fI<buffer>\fR
Seconds subtracted from the eviction limit (default 60)
.TP
\fB\-\-singleton\fR \fI<singleton>\fR
Hold the clone\*(Aqs singleton lock of this name while waiting
.TP
\fB\-\-each\-receipt\fR \fI<each\-receipt>\fR
Read one subject per receipt minted under this name, listed again on every poll
.TP
\fB\-\-arg\fR \fI<arg>\fR
The argument key each receipt\*(Aqs suffix is passed as, with \-\-each\-receipt
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIserver\fR>
The server to dispatch to, as a `[[mcp.source]]` names it
.TP
<\fImethod\fR>
The method to poll; it must have a `[[mcp.result]]` row
.TP
[\fIparams\fR]
One JSON argument object per subject; the wait ends when any one\*(Aqs reduction changes
